{{also|Temperament}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|tempérament|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|temperamentum|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtempəɹəmənt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[moderate]] and [[proportionable]] [[mixture]] of elements or ingredients in a [[compound]]; the condition in which elements are mixed in their proper proportions.
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} Any state or condition as determined by the proportion of its ingredients or the manner in which they are mixed; [[consistence]], [[composition]]; [[mixture]].
# a person's normal [[manner]] of [[thinking]], [[behaving]] or [[reacting]]
# a [[tendency]] to become [[irritable]] or [[angry]]
# {{context|music|lang=en}} the [[altering]] of certain [[interval]]s from their [[correct]] [[value]]s in order to [[improve]] the moving from [[key]] to key

